-- title:
--   Every reporting prefix has the prescribed number of children
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,k\in\mathbb N$ with $k<J$, and let $q$ be a global output whose row in each block is a $2h$-element subset of a $512h$-element ground set. For any list $P$ of local subsets, form its child-prefix list by appending each $h$-element subset of row $k$. Then
--
--   $$\bigl|\operatorname{Children}(q,P,k)\bigr|=\binom{2h}{h}.$$
--
--   No length or validity condition on $P$ is needed for this counting statement. It gives the fixed branching factor used by the indexed reporting constructor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBlockChildrenIndexed.lean#L18-L23

